Z||000007||zeusrekning||08-22-2001||08:04 PM||||PS. I'm pretty sure my problem is with the brake booster push rod. You can look at it and tell it has been cut. It is threaded for an adjuster of some sort. The booster and master cyl. look new. I wonder if the previous owners had the same problem and replaced the booster and master cyl. then finally cut the pushrod. I added about a 3/4" threaded rod to it and reassmbled. drove to the store and on the way back my brakes locked up. I had to release fluid from the brake lines at the master cyl. to drive it home. My dad thinks that with the 3/4 addition the pushrod did not retract far enough to release the pressure in the brake lines. If any one here is a member of the vette forum and could post this for me thanks.||||reg||1
